                <pb facs="0189" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg93"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89France/310b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-27T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1926—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>146. According to the Secretary of the Treasury the possible date now mentioned
                    for Congress to adjourn is June 19. He points out that if Congress is to take
                    favorable action before adjournment early approval by French Parliament is
                    important.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
